Go-only live testbed

Go tests are the only live harness. No Python helpers exist in testbed. No new clones are needed.

Why Go only

Containers already provide CycloneDDS plus ROS Jazzy. Go already encodes and decodes the wire:

- XCDR1 String codec in internal/types/cdr.go:83 (NewEncoder), internal/types/cdr.go:348 (WriteString), internal/types/cdr.go:974 (ReadString).
- XCDR1 primitives for the ROS type matrix in internal/types/cdr.go:247 (WriteInt32), internal/types/cdr.go:287 (WriteFloat64), internal/types/cdr.go:214 (WriteBool), plus internal/types/cdr.go:709 (NewDecoder) for all takes.
- SPDP marshal and parse in internal/transports/dds/spdp.go:488 (MarshalAlivePacket) and internal/transports/dds/spdp.go:722 (ParseAnnouncement).
- SEDP marshal and parse in internal/transports/dds/sedp.go:2482 (SerializeSEDPDATA) and internal/transports/dds/sedp.go:2568 (ParseSEDPDATA).
- In memory publish and receive path in internal/transports/dds/datapath.go:215 (NewPublisher) and internal/transports/dds/datapath.go:625 (NewDataReceiver).

Adding Python would duplicate that codec and add a second failure surface. Adding clones would duplicate images that testbed/docker-compose.yml:8-12 already defines.

Run without exec hell

Rules:

- Use os/exec with docker argv plus structured Env. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:218 (DockerArgs) and testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:368 (ExecRun).
- No shell inside the container for ros2 calls. testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:115-123 (ImageEnv) replicates the Jazzy setup as -e flags, so ros2 runs directly as argv. Same pattern in testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:77 (DistroEnv) via testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:110 (DistroDockerArgs).
- Never run compose up per test. ros-jazzy already runs with host networking and sleep infinity per testbed/docker-compose.yml. Tests fail fast or skip when it is absent. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:444 (SkipIfNoPeer) and testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:161 (SkipIfNoDistroPeer).
- Bring the fleet up once: cd testbed && docker compose up -d. Then run Go tests only.

Commands:

  go test ./testbed/unit/... -count=1
  go test -timeout 60m ./testbed/live/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/bench/ -count=1

Plain go test runs the same suites and skips without a peer; -tags live is accepted as a no-op selector.

Live runs need -timeout 60m: the default 10m package timeout fires mid-suite with the peer present. The ros package holds 204 top-level tests and QoS cases budget 30m each (see testbed/live/ros/gate_qos_full_test.go:37); raise the timeout further if the ros matrix still exceeds it.

Per-package matrix (unit first, then live by package):

  go test ./testbed/unit/cli/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/datapath/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/negative/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/ports/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/sedp/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/spdp/... -count=1

  go test ./testbed/live/gates/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/live/cyclone/... -count=1
  go test -timeout 60m ./testbed/live/ros/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/live/cli/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/bench/ -count=1

Skip-when-absent rule: every live test calls SkipIfNoPeer first and type
matrix tests also call SkipIfNoTypeInterface. A missing docker daemon, a
stopped peer, or a missing ros2 interface show type skips cleanly. Failed
wire, payload, or route asserts still fail. See
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:444, testbed/live/helpers/live.go:326,
and testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:161.

Sentinel versus live-ID rule: header types carry the per-run live ID in
frame_id; types without a string field use a fixed sentinel and rely on
per-run topic plus domain isolation. See
testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:44 plus live frame_id at
testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:389, ID creation at
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131, and topic derivation at
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:144. A missing type skips, a publish with
no route fails loudly after the local codec passes
(testbed/live/helpers/live.go:403-408), and backend errors fail
(testbed/live/helpers/live.go:379-385).

Domain split

- Pooled domains 70 through 101 host the ROS type matrix on per-run topics, allocated via MustAllocateDomain (testbed/live/helpers/domainpool.go:464, AllocateDomainLease at :196). String round trip on /chatter-derived per-run topics lives in testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go (forward at :107, reverse at :160). The extended matrix for Int32 plus Float64 plus Bool plus geometry plus sensor is pinned in testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:100 (cases) with tests at testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:797 and reuses pooled domains with per-run topic isolation.
- SPDP acceptance runs on allocated exclusive domains, not fixed 48. Pinned in testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go (announcement check at :97, pure-Go acceptance at :379, live acceptance at :421).
- Domain 47 is the serial single-entrypoint live gate in testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:41 (LiveDomain); the pool never hands out 47. The serial file split is testbed/live/serial.sh.
- Domains 43 and 44 are the distro matrix: Humble on 43 (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:46-52), Rolling on 44 (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:54-60).
- Domains 60 through 69 are ephemeral isolation for liveliness and CLI checks (ROS liveliness uses 65 through 69 per testbed/live/ros/gate_liveliness_test.go:35-39), so they never hear pooled or fixed gate domains (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:50-53).
- Only one run per domain plus topic at a time. Multicast groups overlap otherwise.
- Every live run uses a per run live ID for payload isolation. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131 (LiveID) and testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:144 (LiveTopic). Start and assert must reuse the same ID.

File split

Cyclone SPDP and ROS String checks live in different packages:

- testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:379 (TestCycloneGate1SPDPST0NonLocalPureGo) and testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:421 (TestCycloneGate1SPDPST0NonLocalLive) prove SPDP acceptance on an allocated pooled domain with direct UDP only. No ROS topics. No trace files.
- testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:107 (TestROSForwardWeldEchoSeesROSTalker) and testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:160 (TestROSReverseROSEchoSeesWeldPub) prove String payloads on a pooled domain with /chatter-derived per-run topics. No SPDP asserts. Scope is pinned in testbed/live/ros/doc.go.
- testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:100 (cases) with tests at testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:797 proves one live case per type on pooled domains with per-run topics. Each case runs forward (ros2 topic pub to Weld take decoded via NewDecoder) plus reverse (Weld pub to ros2 topic echo). Header types carry the live ID in frame_id (testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:389), other types use a fixed sentinel (testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:44) with topic plus domain isolation. Missing ros2 interface show skips cleanly (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:326). A publish with no route fails loudly (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:403-408); backend errors fail (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:379-385).
- testbed/live/gates/gate1_test.go:32 (TestGate1SPDPAcceptance) and testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:33 plus testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:107 (forward plus reverse) are the serial single-entrypoint equivalents on allocated domains. Shared helpers live in testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:218 (DockerArgs).

Do not mix SPDP wire asserts into ROS payload tests. Do not mix String payload asserts into SPDP tests.

Bulletproof checks

- Prove non local by GUID prefix inequality, not by grepping trace. See testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:97 (checkGateAnnouncement) and testbed/live/gates/gate1_test.go:32.
- Decode with ParseAnnouncement and ParseSEDPDATA, not by grepping trace text. See testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:205 plus internal/transports/dds/spdp.go:722 (ParseAnnouncement) plus internal/transports/dds/sedp.go:2568 (ParseSEDPDATA). Failures count as deserialization failures with zero tolerance in testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:404 and testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:447.
- Bound every docker and weld call with context.WithTimeout, not with the timeout binary. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:368, and testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:107.
- Skip when no daemon or no peer is present. Never fail the suite for a missing container. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:444, testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:161.

Status note

Go tests are the canonical live harness, plus testbed/live/serial.sh as the serial runner for the ROS suites. Gate 0 is offline. Gate 1 proves SPDP acceptance by GUID prefix inequality with zero deserialization failures. Gate 2 forward is green after plain CDR receive (internal/transports/dds/datapath.go:1194) plus SEDP fixes; reverse is green after writer 03c2 (internal/transports/dds/sedp.go:177-182) plus announce loop (internal/transports/dds/sedp.go:1350) plus Heartbeat (internal/transports/dds/backend.go:708). A missed live ID in peer echo fails loudly; backend errors and missing sent: still fail. The type matrix in testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:100 follows the same rule: local XCDR1 codec proof must pass, a publish with no route fails loudly (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:403-408), and ros2 interface show absence skips cleanly (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:326). Full wire record is in Conformance - /docs/conformance.

Bench

testbed/bench/ compares Weld against native ROS 2 on legs L1 weld-weld in process, L1c weld-weld containerized, L2 ros-ros, L3 weld-ros, L4 ros-weld. Except L1, both endpoints are containerized: Weld in the weld container, ROS in ros-jazzy, all host-networked with the Go orchestrator on the host. Default go test runs the P0 smoke on all five legs and skips without fleet. WELD_BENCH_FULL=1 scales up: the P0-P6 payload tiers (64 B control, 1/4 KiB, 64 KiB above the fragmentation boundary at 65515, 256 KiB, 1 MiB), 1-to-5 fanout and 5-to-1 fanin with disjoint seq spaces, an uncapped P1 saturation blast for headroom, and a P1 load-latency sweep from 50 Hz to 100 kHz at 50, 100, 200, 400, 800, 1600, 5000, 10000, 30000, 60000, 100000 Hz on all five legs (headroom rows; the choke point is read off the latency-vs-throughput chart with red loss rings). Sweep alone (fleet up): WELD_BENCH_FULL=1 go test ./testbed/bench/ -run TestBenchSweep -count=1 -timeout 60m. Benchmarks allocate pooled domains 70 through 101 with per-run topics like every live test, so no serial.sh entry is needed. One go test run writes exactly one self-contained HTML (inline SVG charts, blue Weld versus orange ROS) to testbed/logs/, gitignored as bench-*.html. Fairness notes ship in testbed/bench/doc.go: same host, same bytes, pinned reliable plus transient_local plus keep_last depth 100 both sides. Observed scaling (WELD_BENCH_FULL=1, 2026-11-03, 110 rows, exit 0; report bench-20261103-204430-3581965.html, all p50 unless noted): 0% loss on L1 and L4 at every payload tier (64 B through 1 MiB) and every sweep rate (50 Hz through 100 kHz offered); ros-to-ros first drops at 10 kHz (2.6%), containerized legs at 10 kHz (13 to 26%). Latency at 1 KiB while lossless (50 Hz to 5 kHz): weld-to-weld p50 10 to 62% below ros-to-ros (about 50% through 100 to 800 Hz, converging toward 10% at 5 kHz as both take loops saturate). Latency by payload, all 0% loss both sides: 16 to 68% lower p50 from 64 B to 64 KiB and at 1 MiB, parity at 256 KiB (within 4%). Sustained achieved throughput at 1 KiB: weld-to-weld about 11.5k msgs/s, ros-to-ros about 9.0k msgs/s. Container tax (L1 vs L1c): within 15% at 256 B and below, within a few percent elsewhere (about 3% at 1 MiB). Caveats: the ros legs subscribe in Python rclpy, so part of their gap is subscriber-side; above about 1 kHz offered the Weld legs achieve less than offered (route settle on fresh domains, still open); choke onset jitters run to run, so treat 10 kHz as the onset zone, not a cliff.
